+# 02: Scheduled downgrades and interval switches, applied at renewal
+
+**What to build:** A **downgrade** (a different plan with a lower or equal monthly list price) or an **interval switch** on an active subscription becomes the subscription's **scheduled change**. Nothing changes today: nothing is billed, refunded or credited, and `change_plan` returns `None`. The subscription shows the scheduled plan and interval so callers can show what will happen at renewal.
+
+At the next renewal, `renew_due` applies the scheduled change:
+
+- the new **billing period** starts on the old period end and lasts one full scheduled interval;
+- the plan and interval become the scheduled ones, and the scheduled change is cleared;
+- the renewal invoice bills the scheduled plan's full price for that interval.
+
+The change still applies if the scheduled plan was retired after the request. When several missed renewals are caught up, only the first applies the change; the rest renew normally on the new plan.
+
+**Replacing and cancelling.** There is at most one scheduled change. A new downgrade or interval switch request replaces it. Asking for the current plan and interval while something is scheduled cancels the scheduled change and returns `None`; the renewal then continues on the current plan. With nothing scheduled, that request still raises `InvalidPlanChange`.
+
+**Retired plans.** Switching interval while staying on a **retired plan** raises `PlanNotAvailable`. Moving to another active plan is allowed.
+
+Parent spec: `.scratch/plan-changes/spec.md`. Timing rules: ADR-0001.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Prorated upgrade for active subscriptions)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] Pro monthly → Basic returns `None` and issues no invoice. The plan, interval and period are unchanged, and the subscription shows Basic (monthly) as its scheduled change.
+- [x] A different plan with the same monthly price as the current one is treated as a downgrade.
+- [x] At the period end, `renew_due` moves the subscription to Basic, bills Basic's full monthly price, and clears the scheduled change.
+- [x] Monthly → annual: the call returns `None`, and the renewal starts a 12-month period on the old period end, billed at the annual price. Annual → monthly works the same way with a one-month period at the monthly price.
+- [x] A downgrade combined with an interval switch is scheduled as (target plan, target interval) and applied together at renewal.
+- [x] A second request replaces the first: a scheduled downgrade replaced by an interval switch results in only the interval switch at renewal.
+- [x] Asking for the current plan and interval with something scheduled clears it and returns `None`, and the renewal bills the current plan. With nothing scheduled, it raises `InvalidPlanChange`.
+- [x] A scheduled plan retired before the renewal is still applied.
+- [x] Catch-up over several missed periods applies the scheduled change only at the first renewal, and later periods are billed on the new plan and interval.
+- [x] An interval switch on a retired current plan raises `PlanNotAvailable`. A downgrade from a retired plan to an active plan is scheduled normally.
+- [x] Subscriptions created without a scheduled change behave exactly as before. All existing tests still pass.
+
+## Comments
+
