+# 03: Upgrade combined with an interval switch, and upgrades replacing a scheduled change
+
+**What to build:** This ticket covers how an **upgrade** interacts with the **scheduled change**.
+
+- **Upgrade plus interval switch.** When an upgrade request also asks for a different interval, the upgrade happens today and the **interval switch** waits for the next renewal. The upgrade is prorated exactly as in 01, at the *current* interval's prices. The scheduled change becomes (new plan, requested interval), and `renew_due` then starts a full period of the new interval on the new plan at full price.
+- **Plain upgrade.** A plain upgrade (no interval switch) clears any scheduled change, so a customer who scheduled a downgrade and then upgrades is not downgraded at renewal.
+- **What a request is compared to.** Whether a request is an upgrade or a **downgrade** is always judged against the plan the subscription is currently billed on, never the scheduled one.
+- **Net effect.** Every request leaves either nothing scheduled or only what that request implies.
+
+Parent spec: `.scratch/plan-changes/spec.md`. Timing rules: ADR-0001.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Prorated upgrade for active subscriptions), 02 (Scheduled downgrades and interval switches, applied at renewal)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] Basic monthly Jan 15 to Feb 15, changed to Pro annual on Jan 25: the returned invoice has the monthly-price proration (−6.77 and 20.32). The subscription is on Pro monthly with Pro (annual) scheduled.
+- [x] At Feb 15, `renew_due` starts a 12-month Pro period billed at Pro's annual price and clears the scheduled change.
+- [x] A scheduled downgrade followed by a plain upgrade leaves nothing scheduled, and the renewal bills the upgraded plan at the current interval.
+- [x] A scheduled change followed by an upgrade with an interval switch leaves only (new plan, requested interval) scheduled.
+- [x] With Pro → Basic scheduled, a request for a plan priced between Basic and Pro is a downgrade relative to Pro (scheduled, `None` returned), not an upgrade relative to Basic.
+- [x] All behaviour is tested through the public `BillingService` interface. The existing tests still pass.
+
