@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Billing
+
+Subscription billing core: what customers are sold, how their billing periods run, and what they are invoiced.
+
+## Language
+
+### Plans and subscriptions
+
+**Plan**:
+A sellable offering with one list price per interval (monthly and annual).
+_Avoid_: Tier, product, package
+
+**Interval**:
+The length of a subscription's billing period: monthly or annual.
+_Avoid_: Billing cycle, cadence, frequency
+
+**Retired plan**:
+A plan that can no longer be sold; customers already on it keep renewing on it.
+_Avoid_: Deprecated plan, archived plan, inactive plan
+
+**Billing period**:
+The half-open span of days `[start, end)` that one renewal pays for; the next renewal is billed on its end.
+_Avoid_: Cycle, term
+
+**Trial**:
+A free period at the start of a subscription; the first paid billing period begins when it ends.
+
+### Plan changes
+
+**Plan change**:
+A customer's request to move their subscription to another plan, another interval, or both.
+_Avoid_: Plan switch, migration, resubscription
+
+**Upgrade**:
+A plan change to a plan with a higher monthly list price, whatever interval the customer is on or moving to. It takes effect on the day of the request.
+_Avoid_: Plan increase
+
+**Downgrade**:
+A plan change to a different plan with a lower or equal monthly list price. It takes effect at the end of the current billing period.
+
+**Interval switch**:
+A change between monthly and annual billing. On its own it is neither an upgrade nor a downgrade, and it takes effect at the end of the current billing period.
+_Avoid_: Interval change, billing frequency change
+
+**Scheduled change**:
+The single plan and interval a subscription will move to at its next renewal. A new plan change request replaces it.
+_Avoid_: Pending change, queued change
+
+**Proration**:
+Charging an upgrade for only the days left in the current billing period, and crediting the unused days of the old plan, so no day is paid for twice.
+_Avoid_: Partial billing
